:l break050
:break f
-- Stops in the forked thread running f
main
:delete *
-- Resumes the forked thread, which loops forever, and blocks waiting for main
-- to complete. A SIGINT (from the Makefile) is then thrown to the forked
-- thread which was resumed, rather than to main: the forked thread is killed
-- and the :continue keeps waiting for main to complete.
:continue
do { a <- readIORef ticks; threadDelay 500000; b <- readIORef ticks; putStrLn (if a == b then "forked thread stopped" else "forked thread still running") }
